## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to apply multi-tenant isolation, data governance, and IR planning in a Databricks context beyond generic concepts.

## Key Concepts

- Unity Catalog RBAC and object-level permissions
- Tenant-scoped secret scopes and secret management
- Dynamic data masking and access controls for notebooks
- Audit logs and SIEM integration for detection
- Incident response playbooks and metrics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo policy enforcement in app layer
function authorize(user, dataset) {
  if (!user.tenants.includes(dataset.tenant)) throw new Error("Access denied");
  // additional masking rules could apply here
  return dataset;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test isolation guarantees across tenants? 
- What metrics and alerts would you instrument to detect leakage or misuse?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to reason about cross-tenant data isolation, token binding, and incident response in a realistic multi-tenant platform similar to large-scale chat/workspace products.

## Key Concepts

- Least privilege per-automation scopes
- Token binding to tenant identity and audience (aud/iss)
- Short-lived tokens with rapid rotation
- Per-resource RBAC/ACL enforcement
- API gateway policy checks and runtime validation
- Tamper-evident audit logs and a 24h IR playbook

## Code Example

```javascript
// Implementation: verify JWT claims for a request
const jwt = require('jsonwebtoken');
function authorize(token, requiredScope, tenantId) {
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, PUBLIC_KEY, { algorithms:['RS256'] });
  if (payload.aud !== 'automation') return false;
  if (payload.tenant !== tenantId) return false;
  if (!payload.scopes.includes(requiredScope)) return false;
  // ensure token is recent
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you design token rotation and revocation in case of breach?
- What telemetry would you collect to detect automation token abuse?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, production-ready supply chain security controls across multi-cloud Kubernetes, focusing on SBOMs, artifact signing, and rapid IR.

## Key Concepts

- SBOMs and risk scoring
- Code signing with Cosign and KMS-backed keys
- CI secrets scanning
- Image-signature enforcement at admission
- 24h IR playbook and rollback

## Code Example

```javascript
// verify artifact signature (pseudo)
const crypto = require('crypto');
function verifySignature(blob, signature, publicKeyPem) {
  const verify = crypto.createVerify('SHA256');
  verify.update(blob);
  verify.end();
  return verify.verify(publicKeyPem, signature);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate and revoke keys in flight without downtime?
- How would you integrate Sigstore or a private CA with this workflow?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical, beginner-friendly security planning around vendor integrations, token binding, and incident response in a multi-tenant setup.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant isolation
- Audience-bound tokens
- API gateway introspection
- Secrets scanning in CI
- IR playbooks

## Code Example

```javascript
// sample token audience check
function authorize(token, audience, tenantId){
  const payload = jwt.verify(token, process.env.JWT_SECRET, { audience });
  if (payload.tenant_id !== tenantId) throw new Error('Tenant mismatch');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you rotate per-tenant API keys and verify their use in logs?
- What metrics indicate cross-tenant access was prevented?

